gcc: enable -Wtrampolines by default

A nested-function trampoline lives on the stack and needs it executable.
On musl, thread stacks are mapped non-executable, so code that takes the
address of a GNU C nested function -- or passes a Fortran internal
procedure as an actual argument -- works on the main thread and segfaults
in any other thread (verified: exit 139 from a pthread). The only existing
hint is ld's generic "requires executable stack" warning, which names no
source line. Warn at the trampoline instead. Warning only; opt out with
-Wno-trampolines. Same idea as Alpine aports gcc 0007.

--- a/gcc/common.opt	2026-09-24 20:20:54.666830299 +0200
+++ b/gcc/common.opt	2026-09-24 20:21:09.320634296 +0200
@@ -833,7 +833,7 @@
 Warn if a comparison always evaluates to true or false.
 
 Wtrampolines
-Common Var(warn_trampolines) Warning
+Common Var(warn_trampolines) Init(1) Warning
 Warn whenever a trampoline is generated.
 
 Wtrivial-auto-var-init
